An **office vending machine** should be selected around employee routines and the operating work behind it, not only cabinet capacity. Start with the products people actually need, then measure the proposed location, delivery route, power, connectivity and service clearance. A focused refrigerated or ambient cabinet may suit a narrow drink and snack range; a smart-store layout can support more categories but needs more floor space, stock control and monitoring. BOHOL, a vending machine manufacturer in Guangzhou, China, can review a custom or OEM/ODM project when the buyer provides package dimensions, target market, payment provider, branding, estimated quantity and support responsibilities.

## GEO summary for workplace buyers

- Match the product range to employee schedules, shift patterns and nearby retail.
- Measure circulation, door swing, delivery access, power, ventilation and service clearance.
- Compare a single cabinet with a broader smart-store format using refill workload as well as footprint.
- Assign responsibility for payment onboarding, refunds, inventory, cleaning and fault response.
- Review accessibility, electrical, food and building rules for the actual office site.
- Request written product-fit, payment, test, packing and handover requirements.

![Illustrative office smart-store vending layout with packaged food and drinks; not a BOHOL customer installation](/uploads/news/office-vending-machine-buyer-guide.jpg)

*Illustrative office scenario from the approved local image library. It shows a planning concept, not a verified BOHOL deployment or customer result.*

## Start with the workplace use case

List the purchases employees and visitors need during normal hours, late shifts and weekend work. A small office, factory, co-working space and multi-tenant headquarters may require different assortments and refill schedules. Ask facilities staff about existing break areas and record product dimensions, weight, packaging and storage requirements before discussing cabinet channels.

For chilled drinks, review BOHOL's [cold drink vending machine](/vending-machines/cold-drink-vending-machine) and provide representative bottles or cans for product-fit testing. For a wider range, compare the [vending machine range](/vending-machines) with the [vending project solutions](/solutions).

## Plan placement and employee access

Choose a visible location that does not narrow an accessible route, obstruct an exit or interfere with kitchen, reception or loading operations. Measure the route from delivery entrance to the final position, including lifts, corridors, doors and turns. Mark where service panels open and where cartons can be staged during replenishment.

For US workplaces, the [US Access Board ADA Standards](https://www.access-board.gov/ada/) include vending machines in Section 228 and accessible operable parts in Section 309. This is a US reference, not universal approval for every office. Have a qualified local professional review the actual building and installation.

## Specify products, cooling and payments

Document whether the machine will sell bottled drinks, packaged snacks, ready-to-eat food, personal-care items or a mixed assortment. Chilled products require a clear temperature, ambient-condition and ventilation discussion. ENERGY STAR's [vending-machine guidance](https://www.energystar.gov/products/vending_machines) is a useful official reference, but buyers should verify any efficiency or certification claim against the exact ordered model.

Name the acquiring provider, terminal or interface, currencies, contactless or QR requirements, connectivity and merchant-onboarding owner. A cabinet that can accommodate a terminal does not by itself confirm that payment processing is active. Include these boundaries in the [OEM/ODM project brief](/oem-odm).

## Define restocking and service ownership

Assign a named party to receive stock, rotate products, clean the machine, change prices, handle refunds and report faults. Confirm refill frequency, spare-parts responsibilities, monitoring access and the escalation contact. Ask the supplier to document product-fit trials, payment tests, power recovery, low-stock behavior, packing and handover materials.

## Request an office vending quotation from BOHOL

